        "created_at": "2013-11-29T16:28:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I got to play two games yesterday and played both as Argent Adept. Really enjoyed it. Some of the most fun was that in the first game I ended up focusing almost entirely on dealing damage! I had out both copies of Scherzo of Frost and Flame and was using the pipes to do four points of damage a turn. Not an amazing feat of damage, for sure, but quite interesting for AA to be doing that instead of other things.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, due to using playtest decks and homebrew decks, of the 13 decks used in our two games, I believe a total of five of them were released decks. That includes my two plays of AA as 2 of those 13. Fun, fun, fun. If you ever find yourself playing w/ Rabit, you might want to try your hand against his homebrew villain and environment. If you dare.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
