        "raw": "<p>One day I hope to live the dream of having Argent go Polyphoric {Harp - Supertonic - [Bell - Syncopated - Subdominant (Vocalize - Syncopated)] Subdominant - [Pipes- Scherzo - Scherzo ]} - [Lyra - Supertonic - &lt;Drum - Syncopated - Scherzo&gt; -Syncopated] }.</p><p>Polyphoric plays Harp which plays Supertonic which plays Bell which plays Subdominant which plays Vocalize, which resolves, destroying one Subdominant.&nbsp; Then Harp plays the other Subdominant which plays Pipes, resolves and destroys.&nbsp; Argent then strums the Lyra during his power phase, and the Lyra plays Supertonic which plays the Drum.&nbsp; You thus get to stack +2 to damage onto yourself, then deal 3 fire, 3 cold, 3 fire, 3 cold, 3 sonic, 3 fire, 3 cold, and 3 sonic, for a total of 24 damage, all of which can be to the same target or up to eight different ones (say hi to Warlord Voss for me).</p><p>With this kind of damage outlay, you can kill Lt. Tamar with the first three blasts, then take out two Gene-Bound Frost-Hounds, two Firesworn and a Banshee, even though all of the Minions are immune to some of your damage.&nbsp; Sure, it takes twelve cards (trashing three of them) and 2 damage to yourself, and Mr. Fixer will make fun of you for having to work that hard (when all he needs is Charge and a Jack Handle plus Grease Monkey Fist and Harmony), but it&#39;s still totally worth it.&nbsp; The best part is that the 2 damage Argent deals to himself comes right <em>before</em> he starts getting +2 to damage.&nbsp; Oh, and you&#39;re also giving the +2 to one other hero, or +1 to two of them.</p><p>Now that&#39;s what I call a pipe dream....</p>",
