        "cooked": "<p>Okay, <a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/article/14130471#14130471\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">I shared</a>. Please post any feedback <a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/thread/1079439/custom-villain-and-environment-lucas-halkom-kad\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">there</a>, though. (Or just enjoy playing with the decks!)</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's when you know you don't play with me enough. I tend to make it a side goal to get set up for damage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It just so rarely happens so impressively. It's kinda like the game in which I drew 7 of Visionary's damage-dealing cards. She was a powerhouse of brutality that game and did virtually nothing else (except her base power)! I've only seen that happen one other time (I'm sure it does) and it's very humorous to see it.</p>\n<p>Now, having side goals is always fun - that one just seems like a good challenge. (My spouse always has a side goal for NightMist to end at maximum hit points, but that's not quite as difficult.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> )</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
